%% Complete Recognition Workflow - MVP Implementation (October 2025)
%% End-to-end flow from Workbench through Recognition Service to Roster

sequenceDiagram
    actor Admin as WordPress Admin
    participant WB as Workbench UI
    participant Hook as useRecognitionJob
    participant Submit as useRecognitionSubmit
    participant Poll as useRecognitionPoll
    participant API as WP REST API
    participant Service as RecognitionService (PHP)
    participant Backend as Recognition API (Remote)
    participant ObsMgr as ObservationManager
    participant Roster as RosterService
    participant Notice as Notice System

    Note over Admin,Notice: Phase 1: Media Selection & Recognition Trigger

    Admin->>WB: Select images in Workbench
    WB->>WB: Update selectedIds state
    Admin->>WB: Click "Run Recognition"
    
    WB->>Hook: runRecognition(selectedIds)
    Hook->>Submit: submitRecognitionJob(ids)
    
    Note over Submit,API: Validation & Request Building
    Submit->>Submit: Validate IDs (toUniqueNumericIds)
    Submit->>Submit: buildApiUrl(/recognition/analyze)
    Submit->>Submit: buildHeaders(nonce)
    
    Submit->>API: POST /recognition/analyze<br/>{attachment_ids: [123, 456]}
    
    Note over API,Backend: Backend Recognition Processing
    API->>Service: analyzeAttachments(ids)
    Service->>Service: fetchAttachmentUrls()
    
    loop For each attachment
        Service->>Backend: POST /api/v0/analyze-scene<br/>{image_url, policy}
        Backend->>Backend: Run face detection
        Backend->>Backend: Generate embeddings
        Backend->>Backend: Match against roster
        Backend-->>Service: SceneAnalysisResult<br/>{faces: [...], matches: [...]}
    end
    
    Service->>ObsMgr: persistObservations(results)
    ObsMgr->>ObsMgr: Store in post_meta<br/>_cat_observations
    
    Service-->>API: RecognitionJobSummary<br/>{jobId, status, stats}
    API-->>Submit: 200 OK {job_id, status}
    
    Submit-->>Hook: Job created successfully
    Hook->>Poll: Start polling (jobId)
    
    Note over Poll,API: Phase 2: Status Polling
    
    loop Every 2 seconds (max 30s)
        Poll->>API: GET /recognition/status/:jobId
        API->>Service: getJobStatus(jobId)
        Service-->>API: {status: 'processing', progress: 50%}
        API-->>Poll: Job status update
        
        alt Job Complete
            Service-->>API: {status: 'completed', results}
            API-->>Poll: Job completed
            Poll->>Poll: Stop polling
            Poll-->>Hook: Job finished
            Hook->>Notice: Success notification
            Notice->>Admin: "Recognition complete: 3 faces found"
        else Job Error
            Service-->>API: {status: 'error', error: message}
            API-->>Poll: Job failed
            Poll->>Poll: Stop polling
            Poll-->>Hook: Job error
            Hook->>Notice: Error notification
            Notice->>Admin: "Recognition failed: timeout"
        else Timeout
            Poll->>Poll: Max attempts reached
            Poll-->>Hook: Polling timeout
            Hook->>Notice: Warning notification
            Notice->>Admin: "Recognition is taking longer than expected"
        end
    end
    
    Note over Admin,Roster: Phase 3: Observation Review
    
    Admin->>WB: Navigate to Roster Manager
    WB->>API: GET /observations?status=needs_review
    API->>ObsMgr: fetchPendingObservations()
    ObsMgr-->>API: Observations list
    API-->>WB: Display pending faces
    
    alt Create New Roster Entry
        Admin->>WB: "Create new person"
        WB->>API: POST /roster<br/>{label, type: 'person', metadata}
        API->>Roster: createAndSync(entry)
        Roster->>Backend: POST /api/v0/roster<br/>Sync embeddings
        Backend-->>Roster: {remote_id: 'abc123'}
        Roster->>ObsMgr: autoAssignPending(remote_id)
        ObsMgr->>ObsMgr: Update observations<br/>status: 'assigned'
        Roster-->>API: Entry created
        API-->>WB: Success + updated observations
        WB->>Notice: Success notification
    else Assign to Existing
        Admin->>WB: Select existing roster entry
        WB->>API: PATCH /observations/:id<br/>{roster_id: 'abc123'}
        API->>ObsMgr: assignObservation(id, roster_id)
        ObsMgr-->>API: Observation assigned
        API-->>WB: Success
    else Dismiss
        Admin->>WB: "Not relevant"
        WB->>API: PATCH /observations/:id<br/>{status: 'dismissed'}
        API->>ObsMgr: dismissObservation(id)
        ObsMgr-->>API: Observation dismissed
        API-->>WB: Success
    end
    
    Note over Admin,Notice: Phase 4: Alt-Text Generation (Future)
    
    Admin->>WB: Select images with resolved observations
    Admin->>WB: "Generate Alt Text"
    WB->>API: POST /alt-text/generate<br/>{attachment_ids, use_observations: true}
    API->>Service: generateAltText(ids, policy)
    Service->>Service: Compose prompt with entities
    Service->>Service: Call LLM provider (GPT/Claude)
    Service->>Service: Update _wp_attachment_image_alt
    Service-->>API: Generation results
    API-->>WB: Alt text updated
    WB->>Notice: Success notification
    Notice->>Admin: "Alt text generated for 5 images"